Date: Mon, 9 Mar 2026 20:59:33 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix: connect RCON via container bridge IP and survive
 daemon restarts

RCON port 25575 is not in the server allocation list, so Docker does not
map it to the host. Connect via the container's bridge network IP instead
of 127.0.0.1 so the RCON bridge can reach the game server.

Extract ConfigureBridge() as a public method on Server so it can be
called from both onBeforeStart() (normal boot) and root.go (Elytra
restart re-attachment). Previously, an Elytra daemon restart would leave
the bridge nil for already-running servers until the game server itself
was restarted.

diff --git a/src/cmd/root.go b/src/cmd/root.go
index 9deab4d..c168cc1 100644
--- a/src/cmd/root.go
+++ b/src/cmd/root.go
@@ -285,6 +285,11 @@ func rootCmdRun(cmd *cobra.Command, _ []string) {
 				if err := s.Sync(); err != nil {
 					s.Log().WithError(err).Error("failed to re-sync server configuration")
 				}
+
+				// Configure the game bridge for servers that are already running.
+				// Without this, an Elytra restart would leave the bridge nil until
+				// the game server itself is restarted.
+				s.ConfigureBridge()
 			}
 		})
 	}
